  "content": {
    "id": "p30-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "In a garden, $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the area is used for vegetables and $\\frac{2}{5}$ for flowers and plants. If the rest of the garden consists of lawns, what fraction of the garden is occupied by lawns?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{4}{15}$",
      "worked": "The LCM of $3$ and $5$ is $15$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{2}{5}&=\\frac{5}{15}+\\frac{6}{15}\\\\\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{2}{5}&=\\frac{11}{15}\\\\1-\\frac{11}{15}&=\\frac{15}{15}-\\frac{11}{15}\\\\1-\\frac{11}{15}&=\\frac{4}{15}\\end{align*}$$\n\nLawns occupy $\\frac{4}{15}$ of the garden.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
